+Also called: Fraedrich stripe decoding, Stripe-based Block Decompression (Fraedrich), Stripe-based On-the-fly Decoding (Fraedrich et al.) [S1, S2]
 
 ## Overview
-Stripe-based On-the-fly Decoding is a general approach for applying sequential data compression schemes to blocks of data, decoded on-the-fly by the GPU in a single render pass by decomposing blocks into parallel stripes [S1, S2]. Unlike [Compression Domain Rendering](960-compression-domain-rendering.md), which often operates directly in the transform domain, or [CPU-Based Block Decompression](7197-cpu-based-block-decompression.md), which offloads decompression to the host, this method performs decompression entirely on the GPU [S1, S2], integrating with the [Deferred Filtering Architecture for Compressed Volumes](857-deferred-filtering-architecture-for-compressed-volumes.md) [Parent].
+Stripe-based On-the-fly Decoding is a general approach for applying sequential data compression schemes to blocks of data, decoded on-the-fly by the GPU in a single render pass by decomposing blocks into parallel stripes [S1, S2]. Unlike [Compression Domain Rendering](960-compression-domain-rendering.md), which often operates directly in the transform domain, or [CPU-Based Block Decompression](7197-cpu-based-block-decompression.md), which offloads decompression to the host, this method performs decompression entirely on the GPU [S1, S2]. It integrates with deferred rendering architectures [Parent, S1, S2].
 
